IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nfp-rules`

§ `Tests`

new MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 7 2020
old MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 7 2012
conf MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 7 2020
notNfp MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 7 2020
onDay MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 14 6 2013
dayBefore MEANS `Agreement clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, Date 13 6 2013

#ASSERT (`the clause position for` new)'s `prohibited content`
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` new)'s `void from` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2020)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` new)'s `the agency breached s 4(1)`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the clause position for` new)'s `earlier accrued rights survive`)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` old)'s `void from` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 6 2013)
#ASSERT NOT ((`the clause position for` old)'s `the agency breached s 4(1)`)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` old)'s `earlier accrued rights survive`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the clause position for` conf)'s `prohibited content`)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` conf)'s `void from` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT ((`the clause position for` notNfp)'s `prohibited content`)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` onDay)'s `the agency breached s 4(1)`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the clause position for` dayBefore)'s `the agency breached s 4(1)`)
#ASSERT (`the clause position for` dayBefore)'s `void from` EQUALS JUST (Date 14 6 2013)
